OpenStreetMap data
------------------
device/data/limits.bin is a road speed-limit pack derived from OpenStreetMap
data covering Cairo, Ismailia and the road between them. It is built by
platform/apps/api/scripts/build_speed_limits.py.

  (c) OpenStreetMap contributors
  https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

OpenStreetMap data is available under the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0:
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

limits.bin is a Derivative Database under the ODbL and is distributed under
the ODbL 1.0, not under the MIT License. If you publicly use or redistribute
it, or a database derived from it, you must keep this attribution and offer
that database under the ODbL.

The synthetic fixtures in device/test/host/ contain made-up roads and no
OpenStreetMap data.

Map tiles
---------
The app and the admin website display map tiles from tile.openstreetmap.org
with the attribution "(c) OpenStreetMap contributors". Use of those tiles is
subject to the OpenStreetMap Foundation tile usage policy:
https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/tiles/
Heavy or production use should switch to another tile provider.

